From 351cea207dbc24b54ef0451e4a9f4002cee98c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:26:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 44/63] native: a refused page plan names the engine's own
 window and what would fit, for the recipe to act on

On KV pages the plan sets the engine's own --context window of pages aside first, then needs a fixed part and a page
for each other stream. Its TooMany refusal named only the second part ("--parallel 4 needs 1.12 GiB for its other
streams' fixed parts ... and the CUDA memory budget leaves 6.21 GiB"), which read as if 6.21 GiB should hold 1.12.

Every refused paged plan now says what it lacks and what would fit, in one clause start scripts can parse:

  --parallel 4 needs 1.12 GiB for its other streams' fixed parts, state runs and a page each beside the engine's own
  864256-token window (5.14 GiB of KV pages), and the CUDA memory budget leaves 6.21 GiB: 0.04 GiB short; fits:
  --parallel 3, TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=3.95 (now 4.00), --context 857080

- --parallel: the most streams this room serves as it is (none when not even the engine's own window fits);
- TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB: the largest reserve at which the asked streams fit at this --context, rounded down
  to a hundredth (none below the engine's floor, or when TENSORFOLD_CUDA_MEMORY_LIMIT_GB bounds the room);
- --context: the largest window at which they fit at this reserve (on pages only; buffers sized by the capacity
  shrink with it, so it errs on the safe side).
The words before ": <short> GiB short" are unchanged, so existing greps still match; the NoStream refusal on pages
gets the same clause (--parallel none). The values come from the plan's own arithmetic; free memory moves with other
programs on the card, so a script should leave a margin.

Test (kv merge, test-kv-merge-host): production's refusal line exactly, then each named value set alone serves all
four streams (the reserve to its hundredth, the --context to a page), a floor or memory limit names no reserve, a
room under one window names no --parallel, and a family whose own window is in the model's bytes has no --context.

